      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There isn't a single magical threshold, as the response is usually a gradual shift rather than an on/off switch. Consistent, deep breathing helps \"train\" the vagus nerve to be more responsive, lowering your baseline stress reactivity over time. With practice, you find it easier to nudge your body across that critical point where the calming signals outweigh the stress signals.",
